hey friends welcome back to the deep  dive snippet this is a little clip from  my interview with mike mayer who's a  breathwork coach and we're talking all  about the dangers of being a mouth  breather i actually did an experiment  last year where i taped my mouth shut  for 30 days while sleeping and that is  something i still do to this day because  it helps me sleep better at night it  helps me wake up with a less dry mouth  and so this is a thing that i've  generally taken away from this like  breathwork stuff when i tried it last  year but yeah let's roll the clip but we  talk about the dangers of mouth  breathing so a few months ago i read the  book breath by james nestor or rather  listen to the  and basically every single chapter in  that book talks about how mouth  breathing is like you know  the coming of satan  there's all of these negative effects of  mouth breathing and he kind of talks  about how  mouth breathing is bad for your jawline  mouth breathing is bad for like  basically basically everything  imaginable um  is that is that legit is mouth breathing  like actually killing us as james nestor  would potentially have us believe  you know you you look at the experiment  he did where he bunged his nose up with  two ear plugs for 10 days he looked  really bad at the end of those 10 days i  think very quickly within the first day  or so his blood pressure had gone up x  amount of points  his sleep was impacted and then i think  he said you know something like 30 of  the american population are breathing  like this all the time and then when he  took those earplugs out of his nose him  and anders olsen i've interviewed both  of them actually um when he took those  earplugs out of his nose i get i think  it was within a matter of hours his  blood pressure started to come back down  again and started to feel more himself  so again is it is it that bad if it's a  breathing exercise i would say no go go  and have some fun with the breathing  exercises but the thing is if most of us  are chronically hyperventilating all the  time we need to get that foundation  fixed first before we stop playing with  the sexy stuff with the big breathing  exercises because that's the stuff  that's going to make sure that we're in  a better place because if you take for  example  you know that wim hof breathing which is  30 big breaths in and then a pause that  is known as a stressor it's like going  to the gym you're stressing yourself out  and there's some benefits to that but if  you're already stressed because you've  been mouth breathing  all day i don't think it's the right  thing for you then to go and do some  more hyperventilation i think we need to  do it the other way let's get our  baseline right let's get it secure and  then once it's in a good place we can  then start to play with them okay  so um  let's say someone someone watching or  listening to this is like all right cool  i'm sold i want to do this nose  breathing rather than mouth breathing  thing are there any  are there any tangible benefits they  would get within a reasonable amount of  time or is it like i don't know taking  supplements where it's like oh i know i  probably should do this just so my body  is b12 levels or a baseline but i'm not  really going to notice  a real difference yeah yeah well by the  way i feel like that about turmeric i've  been taking tumor for two years although  what am i doing here with this bloody  tune brick um so so i i was a chronic  mouth breather and there are some  measurements that you can do so one of  them is um uh well patrick mcewen the  author of the oxygen advantage calls  maximum uh breathlessness test so what  that is that is you because it's always  good to measure isn't it you wanna be  able to measure and track your things  and so what you do is you do a normal  breath in normal breath out your cap and  then you walk um and you count the steps  you can walk and you make a note of that  and another one is you do a breath in  breath out hold and you wait till the  first impulse to breathe happens and  that gives you two numbers so you can  start to track that but let's talk about  what are some of the benefits um and i  think it's about flipping on its head  sometimes so what are the problems  because  here's the thing you know i um i like a  bit of grounding i saw a documentary  about ground and how important it is  that our body touches the earth and this  is a whole other conversation you know  we're the first animal that's removed  our body from the planet which is really  bad you know put insulation on our shoes  and actually you can measure the the  kind of um  electromagnetic static in your body uh  when you touch the earth it kind of  falls down and blood moves better it's a  wonderful documentary  but we're these people that that  kind of expect a big benefit but  actually a lot of us bringing us back to  baseline to be not to be that chimpanzee  with a can of coke with a poor posture  it's more about let's just get us to how  nature intended us to be as opposed to  oh there's loads and loads i'm going to  feel like i'm superman well you might  get some of that but if you're a really  poor breather you might not even know  what good breathing feels like until you  do it i drive people mad because when  i'm breathing when i'm talking i'll i'll  take a normal breath in through the nose  now to carry on the conversation um  because i want to keep that kind of good  habits going so some benefits then so  let's let's break some of this down so  um there are some breathing exercises  that can improve your heart rate  variability and some studies on that so  there's one breathing exercise called  coherence breathing  and that heart rate variability is the  the gap between the beats and they say  that the kind of the variability of  those beats kind of signifies like good  health  sleep is a huge one so probably my  favorite benefit of good breathing i  know you've done mouth taping um and  if you are mouth breathing in the night  which so many of us are because remember  if we're mouth breathing in the gym and  mouth breathing while we're recording  videos and all that sort of stuff and we  talk all day we might be talking all day  and doing different things then there's  a good chance that you might be going to  mouth at some point in the night  now what does that what's the problem  with that well you're never going to get  into the deeper levels of sleep if  you're a mouth breather  and then we know then that poor sleep is  associated with an increased risk of  diabetes cancers high blood pressure um  you know i uh before i mouth taped i was  a frequent weir in the night and i just  thought that was normal and then the  minute i started the matter is i'm not  going for wee anymore i'm like what's  going on there and it's because our body  is releasing the right amount of kind of  hormones and suppressing the feelings of  going to the toilet and that sort of  thing and you get a better night's sleep  and be interesting to know your thoughts  on how you experience it because for me  it took me a couple of months it was so  bloody unnatural to have something on my  mouth i would rip it off but i  persisted with it and now my sleep is is  better i wake up more refreshed i don't  have a dry mouth and so sleep you know  in itself if i just said look i've got  this magical pill for you here that's  going to help you sleep better and it's  going to reduce all the risks associated  with sleep or how much does that pill  i'd love to take that and it might be  able to improve your heart rate  variability and it's gonna be able to  lower your blood pressure um and uh  we've not gone to diaphragm yet but  diaphragmatic breathing could help with  lower back issues could help with  digestive issues so there's a whole host  of other mechanical issues which we can  get into  because our diaphragm's not moving  properly as well and again we want to be  a functional efficient breather  okay so plenty of benefits of  nose breathing and i yeah i mean i still  take my mouth  to uh to this day i don't do it on days  like if for example i'm staying over at  my mom's place and i forget to take my  3m surgical tape then i'm like oh okay  cool i guess i'm not mouth taping  tonight but i do find that on days i  don't know i don't know if this like i i  need to actually track the data on this  properly but  i do find that on days where i have  taped my mouth properly and wake up  having not ripped it off i just feel  like it's it's a bit of fat take it off  and like get in the way of like mustache  and beard and stuff yeah once i've done  that i feel like oh i'm actually i  actually feel pretty rested tonight hey  friends thank you so much for watching  if you enjoyed this clip then click here  for the full unedited episode and if you  like that then do please consider  subscribing to the channel it means a  lot thank you so much and have a great  day

